#lang turmeric stringed
;; The RETIRED-TOKEN migration path, and the last file in the suite with a
;; trailing `#lang` token at all.
;;
;; `#lang` takes a single base dialect now; a trailing token is TUR-E0330
;; (errors/lang-trailing-token). `stringed` is the one exception, for one minor
;; line: it was the only token the decommissioned layer axis ever shipped, so
;; it is accepted, warned once (TUR-W0064) and ignored, exactly as GRADUATED[]
;; does for a retired `--enable` name. A file that opted in per-file keeps
;; compiling across the boundary.
;;
;; Two properties, both pinned here: the warning fires (expected.stderr), and
;; the token is still STRIPPED rather than leaked into the body -- the
;; end-of-line consumption that makes that true is independent of what the
;; tokens mean, which is why it outlived the axis.
;;
;; Retire at age-out (0.50.0): with no legal trailing token left, "stripped but
;; not leaked" has no positive case, and this becomes a second `stringed` case
;; under errors/lang-trailing-token.
(defn main [] : int
  (println "trailing #lang layer tokens are stripped, not leaked into the body")
  0)
